edn|n|The act of committing, doing, or performing; the act of perpetrating. ; The act of intrusting; a charge; instructions as to how a trust shall be executed. ; The duty or employment intrusted to any person or persons; a trust; a charge. ; A formal written warrant or authority, granting certain powers or privileges and authorizing or commanding the performance of certain duties. ; A certificate conferring military or naval rank and authority; as, a colonel's commission. ; A company of persons joined in the performance of some duty or the execution of some trust; as, the interstate commerce commission. ; The acting under authority of, or on account of, another. ; The thing to be done as agent for another; as, I have three commissions for the city. ; The brokerage or allowance made to a factor or agent for transacting business for another; as, a commission of ten per cent on sales. See Del credere.	a:bqg,103,5;qaq,91,3~bqg,103,5;qaq,91,3
