ehj|n|The act of comparing; an examination of two or more objects with the view of discovering the resemblances or differences; relative estimate. ; The state of being compared; a relative estimate; also, a state, quality, or relation, admitting of being compared; as, to bring a thing into comparison with another; there is no comparison between them. ; That to which, or with which, a thing is compared, as being equal or like; illustration; similitude. ; The modification, by inflection or otherwise, which the adjective and adverb undergo to denote degrees of quality or quantity; as, little, less, least, are examples of comparison. ; A figure by which one person or thing is compared to another, or the two are considered with regard to some property or quality, which is common to them both; e.g., the lake sparkled like a jewel. ; The faculty of the reflective group which is supposed to perceive resemblances and contrasts.	a:ksu,48,7;ri1,27,1;w2z,2,3~ksu,48,7;w2z,2,3;ri1,27,1	N:237u,9,1~237u,9,1
