ete|v|To shut up; to inclose. ; To include; to comprehend; to shut up together; to embrace. ; To reach as an end of reasoning; to infer, as from premises; to close, as an argument, by inferring; -- sometimes followed by a dependent clause. ; To make a final determination or judgment concerning; to judge; to decide. ; To bring to an end; to close; to finish. ; To bring about as a result; to effect; to make; as, to conclude a bargain. ; To shut off; to restrain; to limit; to estop; to bar; -- generally in the passive; as, the defendant is concluded by his own plea; a judgment concludes the introduction of further evidence argument. ; To come to a termination; to make an end; to close; to end; to terminate. ; To form a final judgment; to reach a decision.	o:3tn,34,2~3tn,34,2
