gkr|n|A tract of land; a region; the territory of an independent nation; (as distinguished from any other region, and with a personal pronoun) the region of one's birth, permanent residence, or citizenship. ; Rural regions, as opposed to a city or town. ; The inhabitants or people of a state or a region; the populace; the public. Hence: (a) One's constituents. (b) The whole body of the electors of state; as, to dissolve Parliament and appeal to the country. ; A jury, as representing the citizens of a country. ; The inhabitants of the district from which a jury is drawn. ; The rock through which a vein runs.	a:tf1,66,10;k1s,58,6;k1p,48,5;1lkm,28,3;kgh,17,14;bvs,16,3;1gpw,8,4;1tcb,3,6;1fwy,1,9~kgh,17,14;tf1,66,10;1fwy,1,9;k1s,58,6;1tcb,3,6;k1p,48,5;1gpw,8,4;bvs,16,3;1lkm,28,3	v:k1s,42,2;k1p,25,1;vjk,10,3;18jl,6,9~18jl,6,9;vjk,10,3;k1s,42,2;k1p,25,1	V:229p,19,5;22a0,17,2~229p,19,5;22a0,17,2	n:yzg,54,34;sat,9,3~yzg,54,34;sat,9,3	N:22a0,52,22;229p,21,6;2bcq,14,8;2bgf,13,4;12zs,11,1;1y56,4,3~22a0,52,22;2bcq,14,8;229p,21,6;2bgf,13,4;1y56,4,3;12zs,11,1
